            -> stk_a port3.0.13 (member 3, 1000BASE-T, a-full a-1000, VLAN 1);
            Modbus/TCP to 10.38.215.10 port 502
  tools   : tools/mb.py (Modbus/TCP client) on tb470, every call as
              mb.py --host 10.38.215.10 --log /tmp/modbus-1008/mb-22653.log [--slave <unit>] ...
            tools/ckcon.py on tb470: /dev/u5 115200 (the stack master's console);
            tools/rc2cfg.py turned the after-setup running-config into stk_a.cfg
  regmap  : (ART library_1359) 13 words per port from 0x5000, ports in order per member;
            Modbus unit id = stack member. Port #1 = port1.0.1 = unit 1, block 0x5000:
            +0 current state, +1 configured state, +2 PoE configuration, +3 PoE data-pairs
            power, +4 PoE spare-pairs power, +5..+8 input bytes, +9..+12 output bytes.
            State word = 4 nibbles [state, duplex, polarity, speed]: state 0 down / F up;
            duplex 0 auto 1 full 2 half; polarity 0 auto 1 mdi 2 mdix;
            speed 0 auto 1 10 2 100 3 1000 4 10000.

